    {
      "id": "q79nuri",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is anything that possesses mass and occupies physical space.",
        "The primary states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas, each exhibiting distinct physical properties.",
        "Density is defined as mass per unit volume and directly affects buoyancy.",
        "Elasticity is the property of a material to regain its original shape and size after the removal of deforming forces.",
        "Pressure is defined as force applied perpendicular to the surface of an object per unit area."
      ],
      "id": "00rhojo"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s8cekze",
      "content": "• Matter is anything that has mass and occupies space."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zqa4wjo",
      "content": "• It is made up of tiny particles called atoms and molecules."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lc7bfi3",
      "content": "• Matter exists in different forms in nature."
    },
    {
      "id": "grssm5r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. States of Matter"
    },
    {
      "id": "rouiqyl",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>State</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Properties</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Solid</p>",
            "<p>Fixed shape and volume</p>",
            "<p>Iron, wood, ice</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Liquid</p>",
            "<p>Fixed volume but no fixed shape</p>",
            "<p>Water, oil, milk</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gas</p>",
            "<p>No fixed shape or volume</p>",
            "<p>Air, oxygen, carbon dioxide</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rqtpwk9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Physical Properties of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t20cqsg",
      "content": "• Mass – amount of matter in a substance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gqi2e3h",
      "content": "• Volume – space occupied by matter."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Matter and Its Properties",
      "id": "yq7ob7o"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "76vqitq",
      "content": "• Density – mass per unit volume."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bcrwj8f",
      "content": "• Elasticity – ability of a material to regain its original shape."
    },
    {
      "id": "4d6z9sm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Changes in States of Matter"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28tqhl",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Process</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Melting</p>",
            "<p>Solid changes into liquid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Freezing</p>",
            "<p>Liquid changes into solid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Evaporation</p>",
            "<p>Liquid changes into gas</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Condensation</p>",
            "<p>Gas changes into liquid</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sublimation</p>",
            "<p>Solid changes directly into gas</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jv4qc7u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Density"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ig2sm5u",
      "content": "Density is defined as mass per unit volume."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Property",
        "Solid",
        "Liquid",
        "Gas"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Shape and Volume",
          "Definite shape and volume",
          "Indefinite shape, definite volume",
          "Indefinite shape and volume"
        ],
        [
          "Intermolecular Force",
          "Very Strong",
          "Moderate",
          "Very Weak"
        ],
        [
          "Compressibility",
          "Negligible",
          "Low",
          "High"
        ],
        [
          "Fluidity / Rigidity",
          "Rigid",
          "Can flow",
          "Flows freely"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "9sdw8dj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qrmrwna",
      "content": "Formula: Density = Mass / Volume"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "thcedrg",
      "content": "SI Unit of Density = kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "id": "t14x8d1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Elasticity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j61qkxr",
      "content": "Elasticity is the property of a material to regain its original shape after deformation when the external force is removed."
    },
    {
      "id": "go4yvke",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Pressure"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wrtqsy3",
      "content": "Pressure is defined as force acting per unit area."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lqmi9ue",
      "content": "Formula: Pressure = Force / Area"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "46x3xem",
      "content": "SI Unit = Pascal (Pa)"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Water reaches its maximum density at 4°C, an anomalous behavior frequently asked in exams.",
        "Hooke's Law states that within the elastic limit, stress is directly proportional to strain.",
        "Atmospheric pressure decreases with increasing altitude, which causes a lower boiling point of water at high elevations.",
        "The SI unit of pressure is Pascal (Pa), equivalent to 1 Newton per square meter (N/m²)."
      ],
      "id": "20638mf"
    },
    {
      "id": "yrpw5sv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zsqi74r",
      "content": "• Matter has mass and occupies space."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zdmhhdc",
      "content": "• Density = Mass / Volume."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bil3h83",
      "content": "• SI unit of pressure is Pascal."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9a0m0xv",
      "content": "• There are three main states of matter: solid, liquid and gas."
    }
  ],
